# Architecture

## State management — MVIKotlin

Each feature exposes a `Store` through `<feature>/api/store/<Feature>Store.kt` and implements it under `<feature>/impl/domain` with three classes:

- `<Feature>StoreFactory` — assembles `Store<Intent, State, Label>` via the injected `StoreFactory` (provided by `core/mvikotlin/di/CoreMVIKotlinModule.kt` as `LoggingStoreFactory(DefaultStoreFactory())` wired through Napier).
- `<Feature>Executor` — extends `core/mvikotlin/BaseExecutor<Intent, Action, State, Message, Label>`. Handles `Intent`s from the UI and `Action`s from the Bootstrapper; dispatches `Message`s to the Reducer and publishes `Label`s for one-shot side effects.
- `<Feature>Reducer` — `Reducer<State, Message>`; pure `State.copy(...)`.

`Action` and `Message` sealed types live inside the `StoreFactory` as `internal` companions.

### Presentation layer

- `<Feature>ViewModel` extends `core/presentation/viewmodel/BaseViewModel<UiState, UiLabel>` (which extends `androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel` and exposes `state: CStateFlow<State>` + `label: CFlow<Label>` for the iOS contract via moko-mvvm).
- `bindAndStart { store.states.mapNotNull(stateMapper::map) bindTo ::acceptState; store.labels.mapNotNull(labelMapper::map) bindTo ::acceptLabel }` in `init`.
- Public callbacks delegate to `store.accept(Intent.X)`.
- `onCleared { store.dispose(); super.onCleared() }` is mandatory — the Store does not auto-dispose with the ViewModel.

### UI layer

- `<Feature>Screen` consumes the VM via `koinViewModel<Feature>ViewModel()`.
- `state by vm.state.collectAsState()` + `LaunchedEffect(vm) { vm.label.collect { ... } }`.
- Compose-side state mirrors (e.g., dialog visibility, text-field local mirror) live in `remember` / `rememberSaveable`.

### Visibility

- `Store`, `Intent`, `State`, `Label` — public (the Store API).
- `StoreFactory`, `Executor`, `Reducer`, `Action`, `Message` — `internal`.
- Mapper interfaces public, `Impl` classes `internal`.
- `<Feature>ImplModule` (`<feature>/impl/di/`) is the only Koin entry consumed by `appModule`.

Loading lives in `Store.State.isLoading: Boolean`. Errors in `Store.State.isError: Boolean`. One-shot effects (navigation, dialogs) flow through `Label`.

## Koin DI

Core bindings live in `core/di/AppModule.kt`; per-feature bindings live in `<feature>/impl/di/<Feature>ImplModule.kt` and are aggregated by `appModule`. The `core/mvikotlin/di/CoreMVIKotlinModule.kt` module exposes `StoreFactory`.

- `single<T> { ... }` for clients (Apollo, Supabase), datasources, repositories.
- `factory { <Feature>StoreFactory(get(), ...).create() }` to expose a feature `Store` (the StoreFactory itself is `internal` and lives in the same module).
- `viewModelOf(::SomeViewModel)` for view-models (via `koin-compose-viewmodel`).
- `singleOf(::Impl) bind Api::class` to expose mappers and other interface-backed services.

Resolve dependencies:
- In classes (datasources, repos, StoreFactories, executors, view-models): via **constructor parameters**. Koin wires them automatically. No `get()` inside class bodies.
- In composables: `val vm: GuidesViewModel = koinViewModel()`.
- Avoid `KoinPlatform.getKoin()` / `get()` outside DI module — that re-introduces service-locator pattern.

`core/di/Koin.kt#initKoin(appDeclaration)` is the single entry point. It is idempotent (`KoinPlatform.getKoinOrNull()` guard). Called from:
- `AndroidApp.onCreate` with `androidContext(this)`.
- `jvmMain/main.kt` before `application { }`.
- iOS `MainViewController` factory inside `ComposeUIViewController(configure = { initKoin() })`.

`ImageLoader` (Coil 3) is **not** in Koin — it requires `PlatformContext` from Compose and is built inside `App.kt` then exposed via `LocalImageLoader`.

## Compose Navigation

`navigation/AppScreens.kt` defines a sealed class with `route: String` per screen. Navigation uses `compose-navigation`'s `NavHost` + `NavController`.

```kotlin
sealed class AppScreens(val route: String) {
    data object Guides : AppScreens("guides")
    data object DetailGuide : AppScreens("detail_guide/{guideId}")
}
```

`LocalNavHost` is a `staticCompositionLocalOf<NavHostController>` so descendants can navigate without prop drilling. Avoid passing `NavController` through composables when `LocalNavHost.current` is sufficient.

When migrating to type-safe routes (`@Serializable` data objects), do it project-wide in one PR — partial migration leads to mixed-API breakage.

## Build conventions

Every `:feature-X:{api,impl,presentation,ui}` submodule applies exactly one plugin: `id("kmp-feature-setup")` (plus `id("json-serialization")` on `:impl` modules that read JSON). The plugin selects auto-wiring by submodule name — name must be one of `api`/`impl`/`presentation`/`ui`, otherwise the build fails.

Auto-wired by `kmp-feature-setup` (do **not** redeclare in the module's `build.gradle.kts`):

| Submodule | `commonMain` | Other |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `api` | `api(:core-domain)`, `api(mvikotlin.core)` | — |
| `impl` | `api(<feature>:api)`, `implementation(:common, :core-domain, :core-presentation, koin.core, napier)` | `commonTest: implementation(mvikotlin.coroutines)` |
| `presentation` | `api(<feature>:api)`, `api(:core-presentation)`, `implementation(:core-domain, :common, koin.core, koin.compose.viewmodel)` | — |
| `ui` | applies `compose-multiplatform-setup`; `api(<feature>:presentation)`, `implementation(:common, :common-resources, :common-ui, :core-domain, :core-navigation, compose.material3, compose.ui.tooling.preview, koin.compose, koin.compose.viewmodel)` | `androidMain: implementation(compose.ui.tooling)` |

Feature-specific dependencies (anything outside the table above) **stay in the module's `build.gradle.kts`**:

- `:impl` reaches into `:core-network` / `:core-storage` / `:core-resources` only if that feature talks to those layers (`:feature-guides:impl` declares `:core-network` + `:core-resources`).
- `:ui` adds extras like `compose.materialIconsExtended` (deprecated, pinned to 1.7.3 — flagged for migration to Material Symbols) feature-by-feature.

Do not apply `kmp-library` directly to a feature submodule — `kmp-feature-setup` applies it transitively. Apply `kmp-library` only to `:common*` / `:core-*` (which are single-purpose KMP libraries, not feature splits).
